title: "B4-BEC-Lambda-Bridge"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-11
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Kretski
    given-names: Dimitar
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5108-2243"
    affiliation: "Center for Hydro- and Aerodynamics, Bulgarian Academy of Sciences"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kretski/B4-BEC-Lambda-Bridge"
abstract: "Research code for testing whether an emergent dispersion correction of an effective two-scalar field theory (B4 EFT) can be generated by a heavy-mediator UV completion or reproduced by a two-component Bose-Einstein condensate. Includes the exact Proca spectrum factorisation, leading k^2 dispersion coefficients, and a tested mean-field Bogoliubov-de Gennes dispersion module. Status: exploratory; no BEC-B4 operator correspondence is established, and the Proca realisation is documented as a negative result."
keywords:
  - effective field theory
  - Bose-Einstein condensate
  - Bogoliubov-de Gennes
  - dispersion
  - analogue gravity
